{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage","id":420806,"title":"Is there any connection between the Fall of Werewolf and the Fall of Mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-26T16:32:54-08:00","id":420806,"title":"Is there any connection between the Fall of Werewolf and the Fall of Mage?","content":"Been a while since I read the books so forgive any misremembering on my part, but here's how I remember it:<br /> <br /> One myth (from Mage) has a golden age in which primal beings (dragons) benevolently ruled over mankind and taught humanity their secrets. In those days, the physical world and the Supernal were much more closely connected if not identical. Those who learned these secrets were the first mages. However after some time they had to leave and the greatest mages ascended to the heavens where the dragons once flew, via a golden ladder. Once they arrived, they had control over reality. But there was a great war over how to rule,and the ladder was shattered in the process, severing the earth from the Supernal and creating a great abyss in between.<br /> <br /> The other myth (from Werewolf) says that there was a golden age in which a primal being (Father Wolf) benevolently ruled over his children, the werewolves. In those days, the physical world and the Shadow were not separated. However after some time Father Wolf had to die and one group of his children slew him, taking on his mantle as predators of the spirit world. In the process, the earth was severed from the Shadow. But those who chose not to slay Father Wolf declared an eternal war on those who did.<br /> <br /> The parallels are so strong I can't imagine that the writers didn't do it intentionally. The question is, is this a matter of a pattern repeating itself, or two perspectives on the same event?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:42:25-08:00","id":420822,"title":"","content":"No one knows.<br /> <br /> So far as I know, there's no official lore as to how they're related. The similarities are very strong, but you also have to keep in mind that the information on either fall is <i>extremely</i> sketchy and contradictory, so it's hard to say the truth (Atlantis is notorious for having mutually contradictory timelines due to the way it was excised from reality, and elder spirits from Pangaean times tend not to be the most coherent or comprehensible witnesses, in the rare event you can get one to talk).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:44:03-08:00","id":420829,"title":"","content":"In Universe: Nobody knows either way. It is rare for a person to be away of both stories.<br /> <br /> OOC: Possibly a pattern repeating itself, might be intentional. Highly unlikely that the authors will admit to either option.<br /> <br /> Just consider it a plot point like the Arcadia Controversy or the God-Machine Principle. There is enough evidence that says yes for it to be true at your table but there is just as much that says no. Which one makes for the better story?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:50:18-08:00","id":420835,"title":"","content":"An argument could be made for the Fall of Pangaea as a part of the Fall of Atlantis, as the Primal Wild is pulled away from reality and replaced with the divided Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T18:12:46-08:00","id":420940,"title":"","content":"In Mage, the core book at least, the dragons didn't rule over mankind. They lived on an island and some people had dreams of them. Then they left, and the dreams showed the island to be empty so the people went there and further dreams eventually awakened them to their magic. There was much more to it but the dragons were gone by the time anyone went to the island, if they ever existed outside of dreams.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf, the 'golden age' was mostly good for hunters. There were also giant spiders devouring entire villages and massive rats that spread cancer. This world, Pangaea, was separate from Earth but it was much easier to pass from one to the other, there was a place called the Border Marches between them which is what Father Wolf kept guard of. When Father Wolf, the Lord of the Border Marches, died he let out a howl with his final act and the Gauntlet rose, making travel through the Border Marches much more difficult and, to most of humanity, impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-26-2015, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T20:23:22-08:00","id":421134,"title":"","content":"Uhm, in mage, Atlantis was retconned out of reality. It never happened, it's deader than dead, it never existed. <br /> <br /> From the book about the fragments of atlantis, since different atlantean artifacts contradict each other, atlantis has been edited out of reality several times.<br /> <br /> If you take werewolf pangea as actual history and not just legend, since according to blasphemies it doesn't have to be the actual historical truth, conflating the two requires some awkward questions like &quot;Which atlantis that never existed are you looking to combine with it?&quot; <br /> <br /> I mean the Atlantis that was the hypothetical planet Tiamat probably didn't have too much to do with Father Wolf, just off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T20:28:09-08:00","id":421139,"title":"","content":"Well, if you want to pull Imperial Mysteries into this, parts of the universe sometimes gets rewritten by powerful beings or events. Maybe much like Atlantis, Pangaea was an alternate past that never actually existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T20:34:08-08:00","id":421146,"title":"","content":"There's an obvious similarity with a theme of a 'Fall' but they don't seem to have anything to do with each other. If you wanted to mash them together, Pangaea would be the Celestial Ladder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T21:49:38-08:00","id":421228,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think it may have to do with a much broader storytelling pattern. Look at almost any religion's myths, and you will see this same notion of a &quot;golden age destroyed by man's corruption&quot; repeated again and again. (The Bible even does it multiple times - busting Eden, building civilization, having Golden Age, breaking that, having Silver Age, breaking that, having Noah's flood to wipe it all out, and then lots of repentance to get back to the &quot;good old days&quot;.)<br /> <br /> It is, in a sense, the natural reflex of those who are drawn towards religious hierarchies, as religion tends to be the keeper of tradition opposer of social turbulence. The Past Was Better, and Change Is Bad tends to appeal to those who are in the position to write the myths and legends of a culture, so it gets propagated in nearly every world myth that at first, everything was perfect, and every time anyone tried to &quot;improve&quot; anything, it always just made things worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T22:05:54-08:00","id":421274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421134#post421134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Uhm, in mage, Atlantis was retconned out of reality. It never happened, it's deader than dead, it never existed.<br /> <br /> From the book about the fragments of atlantis, since different atlantean artifacts contradict each other, atlantis has been edited out of reality several times.<br /> <br /> If you take werewolf pangea as actual history and not just legend, since according to blasphemies it doesn't have to be the actual historical truth, conflating the two requires some awkward questions like &quot;Which atlantis that never existed are you looking to combine with it?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean the Atlantis that was the hypothetical planet Tiamat probably didn't have too much to do with Father Wolf, just off the top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>My headcanon is that every time a game line gets added it's the result of Supernal shenanigans retconning reality. &quot;What? No, fallen God-Machine angels have always existed. What do you mean you don't remember them being here before mid-2014?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which raises the possibility that (some of) the different Atlantises are connected with the origins of (some of) the different splats. And there are close ties between several of the various otherworlds and some of the splats (Werewolf/Shadow, Sin-Eater/Underworld, Changeling/Arcadia), and strong symbolic resonances between the otherworlds and some of the Supernal realms (Shadow/Primal Wild, Underworld/Stygia, Arcadia/Arcadia). Admittedly, the symmetry is thrown off somewhat by the fact that Spirit is inferior in Stygia, but still, Death being one of the ruling arcana is more important IMO.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, these three connections line up perfectly - Werewolf/Shadow/Primal Wild, Sin-Eater/Underworld/Stygia, Changeling/Arcadia/Arcadia - and leave two gaps corresponding to Aether and Pandemonium, respectively. I suppose one could make the case for Pandemonium lining up with the Dreamtime, but there's no associated splat, and you can't connect Aether to an otherworld or a splat by any stretch AFAIK.<br /> <br /> I consider all this the result of the Ascension War; some ententes are trying to make things all neat and orderly and have a splat/otherworld pair for each Realm while others are vehemently opposed to the idea. Also, someone extremely powerful is clearly <i>very</i> fond of Death given that there are now three major splats associated with it (Sin-Eaters, Vampires, Mummies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T22:21:02-08:00","id":421309,"title":"","content":"I thought Vampires were associated with Hell (&quot;the Damned&quot;)/Pandemonium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T22:26:01-08:00","id":421318,"title":"","content":"You're seeing connections where there are none. The writers didn't do this intentionally. The game lines don't correspond to the supernal realms. To believe that the Mage setting is in some way &quot;truer&quot; than others is missing the point of one of the main setting pillars of Mage - &quot;Beware the dangers of hubris&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T22:28:05-08:00","id":421320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421309#post421309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Vampires were associated with Hell (&quot;the Damned&quot;)/Pandemonium?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ehhh, Pandemonium isn't really &quot;Hell&quot; Hell, y'know? More in the Jacob's Ladder (the movie) sense, in that it's inhabited by the &quot;demons&quot; of your psyche, who cut out the diseased parts of your soul. And vampires are walking corpses that drink the blood of the living and can't abide the touch of sunlight (a powerful symbol of Life). Plus you use Death arcana to work mojo against 'em IIRC, in exactly the same way you use Life magic against regular humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 02-27-2015, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T23:19:47-08:00","id":421364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421318#post421318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're seeing connections where there are none. The writers didn't do this intentionally. The game lines don't correspond to the supernal realms. To believe that the Mage setting is in some way &quot;truer&quot; than others is missing the point of one of the main setting pillars of Mage - &quot;Beware the dangers of hubris&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how it makes Mage's setting any &quot;truer&quot; than any other, it just means they're all playing in a shared cosmos. (In the Changeling core book, the stereotype the elemental seeming has for mages says that they're the real magic, and mages are just the pretenders borrowing the powers of Arcadia.)<br /> <br /> In fact, there's a Changeling splatbook that outright states you actually <i>can</i> find the watchtower of the Lunargent Thorn by passing through the hedge into Arcadia. (It just doesn't do anything but give a few points XP if they study it.) The idea that Changeling Arcadia is related to Supernal Arcadia is canon. From there, it's not just idle speculation that there may be similar correlations, especially since Spirit/Primal Wild and Werewolf seem to meld so well together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 02-27-2015, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T23:24:58-08:00","id":421368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421364#post421364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, there's a Changeling splatbook that outright states you actually <i>can</i> find the watchtower of the Lunargent Thorn by passing through the hedge into Arcadia. (It just doesn't do anything but give a few points XP if they study it.) The idea that Changeling Arcadia is related to Supernal Arcadia is canon. From there, it's not just idle speculation that there may be similar correlations, especially since Spirit/Primal Wild and Werewolf seem to meld so well together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather notably DaveB, the developer of Awakening, has been pretty eager to distance the line from this sort of thing. I think he mention he actually wrote that stuff and regretted it later.<br /> <br /> Anyway, he's been explicit about the two Arcadias <i>not </i>being the same in 2nd edition. I also think it's worth considering that this has always been the Demon problem (That is, not really a problem) just because two things share a name doesn't mean they are the same thing.<br /> <br /> If you want to look for the clarification, I think it's in the thread about the Thyrsus devblog for 2e.<br /> <br /> As an additional note, do whatever you want at your table. If it works for you, great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T23:36:29-08:00","id":421373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421320#post421320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhh, Pandemonium isn't really &quot;Hell&quot; Hell, y'know? More in the Jacob's Ladder (the movie) sense, in that it's inhabited by the &quot;demons&quot; of your psyche, who cut out the diseased parts of your soul. And vampires are walking corpses that drink the blood of the living and can't abide the touch of sunlight (a powerful symbol of Life). Plus you use Death arcana to work mojo against 'em IIRC, in exactly the same way you use Life magic against regular humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think the idea of what &quot;Hell&quot; is has changed as nWoD has evolved, because now, &quot;Hell&quot;'s wherever a Demon sets up shop, and the concept of a &quot;demon&quot; in general is quite different, as well...<br /> <br /> But Vampires aren't really fueled by death, in any event. They're untouched by it. They in fact are noted for how little they tend to have to do with the dead or spirits. They are the ones that most fit the Mastigos archetype, as well. <br /> <br /> Basically, before Mummy overloaded it, you could argue a creature a reflection of each Supernal Realm:<br /> Aether - Promethian (by way of Stealing The Divine Fire)<br /> Pandemonium - Vampire<br /> Arcadia - Changeling<br /> Primal Wild - Werewolf<br /> Stygia - Geist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T23:40:58-08:00","id":421378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421368#post421368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather notably DaveB, the developer of Awakening, has been pretty eager to distance the line from this sort of thing. I think he mention he actually wrote that stuff and regretted it later.<br /> <br /> Anyway, he's been explicit about the two Arcadias <i>not </i>being the same in 2nd edition. I also think it's worth considering that this has always been the Demon problem (That is, not really a problem) just because two things share a name doesn't mean they are the same thing.<br /> <br /> If you want to look for the clarification, I think it's in the thread about the Thyrsus devblog for 2e.<br /> <br /> As an additional note, do whatever you want at your table. If it works for you, great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in general, especially if there's to be a crossover, it <i>kind of</i> helps if everyone isn't working with <i>completely conflicting</i> rules for how the cosmos works. (Especially Hunter, where they basically bulldoze through the rules for all the other gamelines and eliminate powerstats and fuel stats.) Hence, I prefer a single shared universe with each gameline having different scopes of their knowledge to &quot;LOL, physics is completely different for Player A than it is for Player B&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T00:02:57-08:00","id":421406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421373#post421373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I think the idea of what &quot;Hell&quot; is has changed as nWoD has evolved, because now, &quot;Hell&quot;'s wherever a Demon sets up shop, and the concept of a &quot;demon&quot; in general is quite different, as well...</div> </div> </div> </div>It hasn't. Inferno Demons are not the Unchained are not Amkhata, etcetera etcetera. Demon is just a word we're using to describe these things, and Hell is just a word being used to describe different things. Hell, Michigan and Hell, Norway are <i>not </i>the same place, they just have the same name. Maybe they share some characteristics. Both are cold, I'm pretty sure. Both Inferno Demons and the Unchained can make deals of sort that grant boons to people in exchange for things. Just because they both do something similar does not mean they're the same thing.<br /> <br /> It's not a matter of conflicting stuff or anything being confusing. They're different things. If it helps, you might want to, as a player or storyteller, pick different terms. In-universe, the mystery of these things and how often one thing might be confused for another is a staple of the World of Darkness. Hell, it's literally what Mage is about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421378#post421378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, in general, especially if there's to be a crossover, it <i>kind of</i> helps if everyone isn't working with <i>completely conflicting</i> rules for how the cosmos works. (Especially Hunter, where they basically bulldoze through the rules for all the other gamelines and eliminate powerstats and fuel stats.) Hence, I prefer a single shared universe with each gameline having different scopes of their knowledge to &quot;LOL, physics is completely different for Player A than it is for Player B&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The metaphysics of everything are confusing, but I've yet to encounter any instance where running things as written creates a paradox or anything like that. I'm obviously discounting explicit stuff like the different versions of VII, but seriously, where do you see it all conflicting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 02-27-2015, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T00:31:02-08:00","id":421443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421406#post421406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It hasn't. Inferno Demons are not the Unchained are not Amkhata, etcetera etcetera. Demon is just a word we're using to describe these things, and Hell is just a word being used to describe different things. Hell, Michigan and Hell, Norway are <i>not </i>the same place, they just have the same name. Maybe they share some characteristics. Both are cold, I'm pretty sure. Both Inferno Demons and the Unchained can make deals of sort that grant boons to people in exchange for things. Just because they both do something similar does not mean they're the same thing.<br /> <br /> It's not a matter of conflicting stuff or anything being confusing. They're different things. If it helps, you might want to, as a player or storyteller, pick different terms. In-universe, the mystery of these things and how often one thing might be confused for another is a staple of the World of Darkness. Hell, it's literally what Mage is about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The metaphysics of everything are confusing, but I've yet to encounter any instance where running things as written creates a paradox or anything like that. I'm obviously discounting explicit stuff like the different versions of VII, but seriously, where do you see it all conflicting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Demon is clearly in its own league, especially since they kept demons that are just a subset of spirits and demons that are robots with the same name.<br /> <br /> As for conflicts, then on the basics, Hunter is clearly playing by different rules, since everything runs on a more streamlined system.<br /> <br /> As for the grand metaphysics, they're generally vague enough that individuals can interpret things as they will (including the outright &quot;here, pick an origin story for the world, it's multiple choice!&quot; for Werewolf) but if you're playing a game of, say, Changeling, they have stories for how all the stuff relating to Arcadia and True Fae came about, and then a giant freakin' hole to explain the fact that there are also werewolves and spirits and other things that Changeling doesn't comport with.<br /> <br /> For that matter, Changeling glamour comes from human emotions and dreams. Spirit essence comes from emotions and dreams. These two things, however, do not interact with each other in any way, and the two types of creatures seem outright blind to one another's existence at times. It kind of begs an explanation why, if there have been Fae and Spirits visiting Earth for time immemorial, they've still somehow never gotten to so much as acknowledging the existence of one another. For that matter, Changelings frequently manipulate the emotional landscape, which SHOULD have a massive impact on spirits and spirit feeding, and have no means to combat spirits or even detect their presence, and werewolf and changeling turfs don't overlap, but there never seems to be a spirit problem for all the things that Changelings do. (Even if glamour harvests screw with essence accumulation, it's heavily implied that Summers, for example, will brew far more anger than they actually harvest...) Needless to say, if you look back and forth between spirits/Werewolf and Changeling, (or try a crossover game,) it seems there's a gap in the explanations. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the deathless Fae DO have a connection to the Underworld and ghosts... for some reason, even though proper ghosts don't and probably can't exist in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> In fact, this thread opened up with a question about how or whether the origin stories of Werewolves and Mages can be told in the same shared space. I mean, at some point, someone's going to TEST these sorts of theories, and those tests will have results, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 02-27-2015, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T02:02:27-08:00","id":421488,"title":"","content":"I don't see why a ghost can't exist in the Hedge, though I can see them not really forming there...it would need to be brought or get really lost.<br /> <br /> Stuff like the Arcadias being the same (or not) and such are cool and interesting, and never going to be confirmed as true. Changeling is chock full of &quot;If you want it to the be same place than...&quot; which is cool. For those who don't want it to be, it isn't, for those who do, it is. To have it be official just limits options, and New WoD is all about modular.<br /> <br /> It IS interesting there are two sorts of Demons (three counting Lilim) who do not seem associated with Pandemonium...there are the Spirit type Demons associated with the Lower Depths and of course the Unchained who are associated with...earth for lack of something better. And the Lilim.<br /> <br /> As for the original question, it does seem to speak of some half-remembered event, which is interesting. &quot;A long time ago, something happened and shit got real. This lesser world is the result. Is a sign things went horribly awry? Or that darkness was contained to the point that it lingers only in the shadows and it was a victory.&quot; Is an interesting question to go poking at and an unlikely one to be answered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T02:04:47-08:00","id":421492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421368#post421368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rather notably DaveB, the developer of Awakening, has been pretty eager to distance the line from this sort of thing. I think he mention he actually wrote that stuff and regretted it later.<br /> <br /> Anyway, he's been explicit about the two Arcadias <i>not </i>being the same in 2nd edition. I also think it's worth considering that this has always been the Demon problem (That is, not really a problem) just because two things share a name doesn't mean they are the same thing.<br /> <br /> If you want to look for the clarification, I think it's in the thread about the Thyrsus devblog for 2e.<br /> <br /> As an additional note, do whatever you want at your table. If it works for you, great.</div> </div> </div> </div>To tie into this, it should be pointed out that now it would be almost impossible to reconcile the two Arcadias as the same place because the Supernal isn't even a proper place, it is more the platonic ideal coding of the fallen world, some things are just able to be symbols and alive at the same time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421443#post421443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, Changeling glamour comes from human emotions and dreams. Spirit essence comes from emotions and dreams. These two things, however, do not interact with each other in any way, and the two types of creatures seem outright blind to one another's existence at times. It kind of begs an explanation why, if there have been Fae and Spirits visiting Earth for time immemorial, they've still somehow never gotten to so much as acknowledging the existence of one another. For that matter, Changelings frequently manipulate the emotional landscape, which SHOULD have a massive impact on spirits and spirit feeding, and have no means to combat spirits or even detect their presence, and werewolf and changeling turfs don't overlap, but there never seems to be a spirit problem for all the things that Changelings do. (Even if glamour harvests screw with essence accumulation, it's heavily implied that Summers, for example, will brew far more anger than they actually harvest...) Needless to say, if you look back and forth between spirits/Werewolf and Changeling, (or try a crossover game,) it seems there's a gap in the explanations.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the deathless Fae DO have a connection to the Underworld and ghosts... for some reason, even though proper ghosts don't and probably can't exist in the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>One explanation someone came up with for the differences between glamour and essence that I liked (and am butchering and getting wrong) was by comparing emotions to a power generator. A generator produces electricity, but it also gives off heat as a byproduct. Also, the Fae probably do have spirit contracts because if they didn't they would have trouble even acknowledging or notcing them if they didn't and spirits are such a big part of the world that to not have a contract with them would be a ludicrous oversight on their part. For example, they don't have a contract with Pyros so they barely notice the presence of a Promethean unless the Promethean gets up in their face or something like that.As for an explanation on why it never really comes up, not very many spirits are in the physical world and changelings are very good at looking like mundane humans even under extreme supernatural scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Of course all of this is just headcanon, but I think it makes sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T02:07:55-08:00","id":421495,"title":"","content":"About the two Falls, I think it's two different remains of the same event, with the distortion given by time passing. There is just too much similarities between the symbolic of the Fall, and even the Abyssal beings and the Idigam are very alike.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421443#post421443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meanwhile, the deathless Fae DO have a connection to the Underworld and ghosts... for some reason, even though proper ghosts don't and probably can't exist in the Hedge.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>False, it was stated in i-don't-remember-wich supplement that given that the Hedge can open in all the other realms, often entities entre in it. Humans get lost, and if they survive enough time they are captured and become changelings, wherease the ephemeral entities (fully corporal in the Hedge) tend to become hobgoblins with the glamour exposure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T02:35:55-08:00","id":421519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421368#post421368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rather notably DaveB, the developer of Awakening, has been pretty eager to distance the line from this sort of thing. I think he mention he actually wrote that stuff and regretted it later.<br /> <br /> Anyway, he's been explicit about the two Arcadias <i>not </i>being the same in 2nd edition. I also think it's worth considering that this has always been the Demon problem (That is, not really a problem) just because two things share a name doesn't mean they are the same thing.<br /> <br /> If you want to look for the clarification, I think it's in the thread about the Thyrsus devblog for 2e.<br /> <br /> As an additional note, do whatever you want at your table. If it works for you, great.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'd be interested and not particularly surprised to find out I was wrong about this, I don't think the position he's laid out is quite that they're definitely not the same, so much as that he used to think they were the probably the same and now thinks they're probably not but it shouldn't be much addressed or made explicit one way or the other.<br /> <br /> There's also a neat thing he wrote on these forums somewhere (I can't find it anymore) when he was in the first mindset about how Arcadia was and wasn't conquered by the Exarchs that I like too much to let go of. I've always preferred that the answer to the tie between the Arcadias be <i>tilt</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T02:45:40-08:00","id":421529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421519#post421519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also a neat thing he wrote on these forums somewhere (I can't find it anymore) when he was in the first mindset about how Arcadia was and wasn't conquered by the Exarchs that I like too much to let go of. I've always preferred that the answer to the tie between the Arcadias be <i>tilt</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The True Fae as presented in Equinox Roads are basically living bunches of symbols (Titles), so it did make sense that they could be Supernal entities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T02:49:10-08:00","id":421530,"title":"","content":"Isn't part of the mythology behind the Aegis Kai Doru that both &quot;falls&quot; are related? I admit is been a long while since the last time I read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T03:18:20-08:00","id":421538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421519#post421519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I'd be interested and not particularly surprised to find out I was wrong about this, I don't think the position he's laid out is quite that they're definitely not the same, so much as that he used to think they were the probably the same and now thinks they're probably not but it shouldn't be much addressed or made explicit one way or the other.<br /> <br /> There's also a neat thing he wrote on these forums somewhere (I can't find it anymore) when he was in the first mindset about how Arcadia was and wasn't conquered by the Exarchs that I like too much to let go of. I've always preferred that the answer to the tie between the Arcadias be <i>tilt</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah. Second edition, they're not the same place. For reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 02-27-2015, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T03:20:43-08:00","id":421540,"title":"","content":"...Poor Dave Brookshaw...<br /> This is 3rd? 4th? time you've had say this in the last week...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T05:16:23-08:00","id":421621,"title":"","content":"Reality has been shattered on at least 3 occasions in the World of Darkness between Mage, Mummy, and Werewolf. There is strong evidence that the Underworld is something of an atrophied organ that no longer serves its original purpose and nobody is sure why, though mages have their hunch that it's tied to the Fall. One of the most often recited lines in relation to Demon and more specifically the God Machine is &quot;<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What rises must fall. What has fallen may rise again.&quot; I'm probably forgetting half a dozen other things.<br /> <br /> This is a broken world.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T05:16:37-08:00","id":421622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421530#post421530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't part of the mythology behind the Aegis Kai Doru that both &quot;falls&quot; are related? I admit is been a long while since the last time I read it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Only if you find the idea of werewolves being the descendants of a minotaur and an undead human bee hive more compelling than any other origin story, or even logic.<br /> <br /> Because seriously, how do you get werewolves out of a minotaur and and a bee woman? <br /> <br /> Not to mention the atlantis relationship never made sense either, for the same reason I always thought the &quot;nameless empire was founded by mages&quot; bit people would suggest in mummy- If you're a mage, why the @#$#$#$ would you bother with relics when as a mage you can make fetishes, enhanced items, enchanted items, and use artifacts? <br /> <br /> Combining relic making with ones native magic item creation abilities, okay, sure, but you don't build a society around something inferior to your native abilities, If people could punch someone to death from miles away there wouldn't be a gun industry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T05:38:18-08:00","id":421633,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, either reality broke once and the different splats have differing accounts of the same event, or it broke multiple times and each splat only noticed the one they had a hand in, somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:02:52-08:00","id":421720,"title":"","content":"It probably broke more than once, if it broke at all.<br /> <br /> Folks can travel through the Gauntlet now, but Werewolves and spirits can't go into the Border Marches anymore, it's sealed to them. And there does seem to be some sort of gap between the Supernal and the material world.<br /> <br /> I guess if you want to force the Platonic stuff to explain the Supernal as true forms, the material world would be the imitations put before the fire, and the Shadow would be the shadows playing on the wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:17:08-08:00","id":421728,"title":"","content":"I'm like 99% sure the bordermarches were a sort of shadow/material hybrid place that existed before the gauntlet split them apart. So it's not so much &quot;sealed&quot; as &quot;destroyed&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:34:40-08:00","id":421740,"title":"","content":"It's still there, we're just unable to do anything with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/316241-wtf-2ed-weekly-discussion-questions-and-answers-part-2?p=329145#post329145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He <i>hunted</i> in the Border Marches pre-murder; instead of a Gauntlet, there was a realm blending the material and Shadow together, that anyone could journey through in select places. His death Howl turned these Border Marches into the Gauntlet. Werewolves like to pretend (&quot;this story is true&quot;) that anything inside was killed or trapped in place forever. This is mostly because werewolves can't move inside it - when you cross over, you experience a few seconds of hanging, paralyzed, in the Gauntlet's grey void before the world you're entering forms around you.<br /> <br /> But sometimes you can see things out of the corner of your eye, or catch an odd scent, while crossing over.<br /> The Gauntlet has life inside it, for a certain value of &quot;life,&quot; that most people treating it as a barrier and not a seperate realm of existence never see. It's part of the esoterica of the nWoD's cosmology, because while werewolves and mages suspect there's something there, and sometimes try to summon Gauntlet entities to varying degrees of success, none of our protagonist supernatural beings deal with them directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:45:13-08:00","id":421747,"title":"","content":"Summoners does present weird trilobite things living there that immediately die if you pull them out. Nonetheless, the quote you just posted outright contradicts your point. The Bordermarches <i>became</i> the Gauntlet. The metaphysical place they occupied still exists, but it's not part of the bordermarches any more because the bordermarches were defined as the place where you could slip from shadow to material easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:50:55-08:00","id":421751,"title":"","content":"It's... questionable. Is the modern-day Gauntlet the ruin of the Bordermarches, or the gaping wound in reality left when the Bordermarches ceased to exist? (Hence why you can't move inside it - it isn't a &quot;place&quot; any more, and has no physical laws.)<br /> <br /> Who knows? Maybe your Pack Elodoth can explain it to you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:16:17-08:00","id":421773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421747#post421747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summoners does present weird trilobite things living there that immediately die if you pull them out. Nonetheless, the quote you just posted outright contradicts your point. The Bordermarches <i>became</i> the Gauntlet. The metaphysical place they occupied still exists, but it's not part of the bordermarches any more because the bordermarches were defined as the place where you could slip from shadow to material easily.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Questionable is right. At this point it's a matter of is a road still a road if the road is closed. I say yes but it's not unreasonable to say otherwise.<br /> <br /> Mages and werewolves and spirits still pass through easily. Even Demons can, though not subtly. The more mundane roads seemed to have been sealed off, as it was implied you could simply walk from the gurihal to the Hisil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:27:08-08:00","id":421781,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out that the story of The Fall of Atlantis and the story of Wolf and Moon are both myths, from very different cultures, neither of which generally view their respective myths as the literal Truth, with the possible exception of a few extreme fundamentalist individuals within either group. You're comparing similarities between what are essentially just-so stories from two very different cultures and drawing the conclusion that they must be describing the same fall. How many real-world cultures have Great Flood myths? The more likely conclusion is that people tell similar stories to explain universal facets of the human condition than that there was a single worldwide flood and all of these cultures are unknowingly telling the story of the same event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-27-2015, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:31:43-08:00","id":421784,"title":"","content":"Well, obviously &quot;they're both bullshit&quot; is an obvious answer but I think we were giving them the benefit of the doubt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:33:01-08:00","id":421786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421784#post421784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, obviously &amp;quot;they're both bullshit&amp;quot; is an obvious answer but I think we were giving them the benefit of the doubt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really my point...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:34:49-08:00","id":421787,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think it might be a case where the actual question to be asked, and possible what was meant is not IS there any connection but what particularly intriguing stories can you make by creating a connection and the particularly nature of said connection.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:53:28-08:00","id":421821,"title":"","content":"It is also a setting where cultural stories can - and perhaps often do - have grains of truth at their core. Just as in reality, as well, people who have flood myths often have to deal with floods as a major source of catastrophe. Volcanoes feature prominently in the world creation myths of those who live near volcanoes.<br /> <br /> I'm partial to the idea of Mythic History being bigger than people can perceive. Hellboy's my go-to source of inspiration in that regard; with a grand, sprawling history whose truth is often hard to grasp because you see small fragments of a bigger whole and never get the full story. Lemuria, Hyperborea, Atlantis, Mu, they all existed and all rewrote the world, but... How? All we see is fragmentary pieces of magical empires that spanned thousands of years, perhaps tens or hundreds of thousands. And throughout this, their reach seems impressive, but we still also have creatures like the Bog Roosh dwelling in the ocean depths and the fae lurking in their hidden places, which do not seem inclined to treat these supposedly great empires as anything at all, much less passing fancies. They don't look down, they don't look up; the world is simply so big that immense magical empires weren't something particularly important to them.<br /> <br /> If there is a Mythic History to the World of Darkness, this is the way I like to use it. The question of &quot;Did Atlantis exist?&quot; is interesting, but Mythic History should never feel like you know all the answers. You should always stumble onto things that make you go &quot;Wait, how does this fit into the big picture?&quot; as the map stretches ever wider and every dark patch you fill in adds a thousand new miles of undiscovered country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:00:10-08:00","id":421831,"title":"","content":"Ok, I think my point got massively misinterpreted. I wasn't trying to say &quot;why even assume they're true&quot; so much as &quot;why assume they're the same event&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:02:28-08:00","id":421836,"title":"","content":"While I've never been the person who loves to put the literal occult on a pedestal and vagueness for it's own sake as well. Reading back on some H.P. Lovecraft recently tends to illuminate to some extent why a &quot;show little and less&quot; approach tends to work over the MAPALLTHETHINGS! approach. In a number of stories there are references to someone getting into the occult mysteries of the setting or whatnot and searching lore and land for things like &quot;Atlantis and Lost Lemuria.&quot;,etc but the stories always move towards, &quot;And all these crazy things proceeded from the drive and desire of said person.&quot; without ever actually dealing one way or the other on if any of that did or didn't exist, or maybe did but was shoved through the cosmic paper shredder,etc. With the mood of Mage in particularly and the general mood of the NWoD. I'd say follow Axelgear's final remarks. The NWoD is turtles all the way down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-27-2015, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:06:02-08:00","id":421845,"title":"","content":"The Werewolf myth has always been interesting to me as a werewolf fan, but even with the few similarities I don't really see it coinciding with the Mage origin story.<br /> <br /> But looking into what we do know about the various myths could suggest other things. For instance Dave Brookshaw pointed out that the Gauntlet may be a 'gaping wound left in reality' after the fall of Father Wolf, providing that story is true, and the fall of the Border Marches, similarly. But if you look around a bit more, tied in with the Maeljin who are currently considered entities of the Inferno, you'll see the myth of the First Wound. According to Werewolf legend, the First Wound is where Father Wolf was killed, and from that act was born the Maeljin of Violence, Thurifuge, who built a palace on or from Father Wolf's bones. Thurifuge is now considered a high-ranking demon of the Inferno, I think Maeljin are around rank 8. So if you wanted you could have a story in your game connecting the Gauntlet and the death of the Border Marches to the Inferno or, from a Mage point of view, the Lower Depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-27-2015, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:54:52-08:00","id":421907,"title":"","content":"Are the Maeljin still associated with the Inferno? New edition and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:56:28-08:00","id":421910,"title":"","content":"We don't know, but it does look like Wound-influenced spirits are separate from normal spirits. There's a banish spirit rite we've seen a first draft of that sends spirits back to the Shadow but Wound-influenced spirits somewhere else. <br /> <br /> 'There are reports that this rite also works on Wounded spirits if conducted in the Wound in question, pushing them out of the Shadow and into...somewhere else.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-27-2015, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T12:56:50-08:00","id":422135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421845#post421845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Werewolf myth has always been interesting to me as a werewolf fan, but even with the few similarities I don't really see it coinciding with the Mage origin story.<br /> <br /> But looking into what we do know about the various myths could suggest other things. For instance Dave Brookshaw pointed out that the Gauntlet may be a 'gaping wound left in reality' after the fall of Father Wolf, providing that story is true, and the fall of the Border Marches, similarly. But if you look around a bit more, tied in with the Maeljin who are currently considered entities of the Inferno, you'll see the myth of the First Wound. According to Werewolf legend, the First Wound is where Father Wolf was killed, and from that act was born the Maeljin of Violence, Thurifuge, who built a palace on or from Father Wolf's bones. Thurifuge is now considered a high-ranking demon of the Inferno, I think Maeljin are around rank 8. So if you wanted you could have a story in your game connecting the Gauntlet and the death of the Border Marches to the Inferno or, from a Mage point of view, the Lower Depths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which reminds me: there seems to be some possible correlation between the Maeljin and/or Demon Princes and the Angels who cursed humanity in the Testament of Marco Singe. With the usual caveats that Marco is an unreliable narrator repeating information from an untrustworthy source, the Demon Princes and Maeljin aren't exactly things that anyone has done a comprehensive empirical study on, etc.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, we have one of the Angels (I think it was Strife) being imprisoned at the &quot;bottom of the world&quot; and a pack of Werewolves in one of the books that found a Maeljin in Antarctica and decided to worship it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T13:10:51-08:00","id":422141,"title":"","content":"I think it just calls them demons there.<br /> <br /> But the Inferno book assigns ranks to demonic entities, the Maeljin are Rank 8, comparable to Dukes and Duchesses but perhaps not the same. They worked off of 9 vices, instead of 7, which always seemed like an odd difference. Princes are Rank 9.<br /> <br /> As I read more about it the Border Marches sounds like the Hedge. Not exactly like but they both exist as worlds-as-pathways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-27-2015, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T13:26:24-08:00","id":422147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422141#post422141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it just calls them demons there.<br /> <br /> But the Inferno book assigns ranks to demonic entities, the Maeljin are Rank 8, comparable to Dukes and Duchesses but perhaps not the same. They worked off of 9 vices, instead of 7, which always seemed like an odd difference. Princes are Rank 9.<br /> <br /> As I read more about it the Border Marches sounds like the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demonology isn't an exact science. I imagine the number of people who've encountered a.Maeljin OR a Demon Prince and survived with sanity and soul intact is extremely small. And since the non-core books aren't canon so much as suggestions, I:m gonna go with &quot;It's not that tidy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, one could consider the Autochthonous Depths as a Hedge-like border realm between the Material plane and the Lower Depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 02-27-2015, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T13:33:30-08:00","id":422157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421373#post421373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I think the idea of what &amp;quot;Hell&amp;quot; is has changed as nWoD has evolved, because now, &amp;quot;Hell&amp;quot;'s wherever a Demon sets up shop, and the concept of a &amp;quot;demon&amp;quot; in general is quite different, as well...<br /> <br /> But Vampires aren't really fueled by death, in any event. They're untouched by it. They in fact are noted for how little they tend to have to do with the dead or spirits. They are the ones that most fit the Mastigos archetype, as well. <br /> <br /> Basically, before Mummy overloaded it, you could argue a creature a reflection of each Supernal Realm:<br /> Aether - Promethian (by way of Stealing The Divine Fire)<br /> Pandemonium - Vampire<br /> Arcadia - Changeling<br /> Primal Wild - Werewolf<br /> Stygia - Geist</div> </div> </div> </div>Read up on what happens to Vampires in the Underworld. It's in the Underworld book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T13:41:13-08:00","id":422180,"title":"","content":"Do you mean the calm due to the lack of blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T13:51:29-08:00","id":422194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422180#post422180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean the calm due to the lack of blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Among other things. They can eat ghosts and a lot of the drawbacks of the Predator's Taint disappear, along with not having to worry about sunlight.<br /> <br /> In a lot of ways, the Underworld is a vampire's ideal habitat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T14:00:27-08:00","id":422201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422180#post422180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean the calm due to the lack of blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a whole river of it down there that they can drink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T15:24:22-08:00","id":422245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422201#post422201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a whole river of it down there that they can drink.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. And yet they never suffer Frenzy.<br /> <br /> I think there's also a bloodline that goes on incorporeal jaunts to the Underworld during torpor or somesuch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 02-27-2015, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T15:47:17-08:00","id":422266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422147#post422147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, one could consider the Autochthonous Depths as a Hedge-like border realm between the Material plane and the Lower Depths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about the Lower Depths as in where (Inferno) Demons come from or Lower Depths as in Dead Dominions? If the former no, not at all. If the latter yes, I agree.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:00:03-08:00","id":422274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422266#post422266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you talking about the Lower Depths as in where (Inferno) Demons come from or Lower Depths as in Dead Dominions? If the former no, not at all. If the latter yes, I agree.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dead Dominions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422141#post422141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it just calls them demons there.<br /> <br /> But the Inferno book assigns ranks to demonic entities, the Maeljin are Rank 8, comparable to Dukes and Duchesses but perhaps not the same. They worked off of 9 vices, instead of 7, which always seemed like an odd difference. Princes are Rank 9.<br /> <br /> As I read more about it the Border Marches sounds like the Hedge. Not exactly like but they both exist as worlds-as-pathways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a vague idea about the each of the various Otherworlds having at some point in metatime been the Golden Road of a no-longer-extant Archmage on the same level as the Oracles, with the border worlds having been their Chantry. Or the Oracles of a previous version of reality. Or something. Anyway, they're abandoned by their original creators now, so they've kinda turned into the equivalent of that house in your neighborhood that's overrun with weeds and inhabited by vermin and squatters.<br /> <br /> In this headcanon, that bit about being able to reach the Tower of the Lunargent Thorn from Changeling Arcadia makes perfect sense if CArcadia was originally an Acanthus Archmage's Golden Road. And the Ocean of Fragments from Underworld? The oldest ghosts appear to end up there inevitably, and nobody knows what happens to them after they lose all their identifiers, including &quot;I am.&quot; But, here's a thought: Maybe they slip through a hole at the bottom and wind up in Stygia as a fresh Shade.<br /> <br /> And if you think about it... maybe the various otherworlds are less the remains of Golden Roads than the fragments of the Golden Ladder? Or is there a difference? Maybe the Golden Ladder was a communal Golden Road erected by multiple Mages acting in concert?<br /> <br /> What happens if you take a five-pointed star, and fold the five arms so that their points touch?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://etc.usf.edu/clipart/43100/43188/pent1_43188_lg.gif\" target=\"_blank\">http://etc.usf.edu/clipart/43100/431...1_43188_lg.gif</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 02-27-2015, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:22:57-08:00","id":422285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422274#post422274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dead Dominions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we agree therefore it clearly is correct. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF000