</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422245#post422245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. And yet they never suffer Frenzy.<br /> <br /> I think there's also a bloodline that goes on incorporeal jaunts to the Underworld during torpor or somesuch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mythologies offers it as an explanation as to why Torpor messes with Kindred so much. While in Torpor, their souls are in the Underworld, (probberly a single Dead Dominion but this predates Geist/Book of the Dead), being connected to their body by a single spiritual thread. Whomever is holding the thread when the physical vampire gets out of Torpor, gets the body. Not your body? Congrats you get a mix of it's memories and yours get a dreamlike quality.<br /> <br /> I don't think they went that way for 2nd/B&amp;S ed but still awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T17:31:18-08:00","id":422349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422312#post422312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mythologies offers it as an explanation as to why Torpor messes with Kindred so much. While in Torpor, their souls are in the Underworld, (probberly a single Dead Dominion but this predates Geist/Book of the Dead), being connected to their body by a single spiritual thread. Whomever is holding the thread when the physical vampire gets out of Torpor, gets the body. Not your body? Congrats you get a mix of it's memories and yours get a dreamlike quality.<br /> <br /> I don't think they went that way for 2nd/B&amp;S ed but still awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's it.<br /> <br /> There's also, IIRC, a bloodline that supposedly ruled a vast empire once, and was able to walk in the sunlight back then (but not anymore). One explanation for it was that this was true in a timeline that's been erased. More Ascension War fuckery?<br /> <br /> I rather like the idea of the various splats as Phenomenal echoes of shit that's going on in the Supernal as the Archmages try to redefine the symbols for humanity. Supernatural fallout, if you will (literally in the case of Zeky Prometheans.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422285#post422285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then we agree therefore it clearly is correct. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Quite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 02-27-2015, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T17:42:03-08:00","id":422364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422266#post422266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you talking about the Lower Depths as in where (Inferno) Demons come from or Lower Depths as in Dead Dominions?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Nota bene</i> that the common English names for Erebus and Tartarus are the <i>Autochthonous</i> Depths and the Lower <i>Mysteries</i>, lest anyone get confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T18:23:19-08:00","id":422380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422364#post422364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Nota bene</i> that the common English names for Erebus and Tartarus are the <i>Autochthonous</i> Depths and the Lower <i>Mysteries</i>, lest anyone get confused.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thankee, I don't actually play the games so my mastery of terms is not that strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T19:50:29-08:00","id":422507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421781#post421781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to point out that the story of The Fall of Atlantis and the story of Wolf and Moon are both myths, from very different cultures, neither of which generally view their respective myths as the literal Truth, with the possible exception of a few extreme fundamentalist individuals within either group. You're comparing similarities between what are essentially just-so stories from two very different cultures and drawing the conclusion that they must be describing the same fall. How many real-world cultures have Great Flood myths? The more likely conclusion is that people tell similar stories to explain universal facets of the human condition than that there was a single worldwide flood and all of these cultures are unknowingly telling the story of the same event.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, a theory of the global flood myth is that it occurred at an early enough period in time (basically, the last Ice Age) that the people who were displaced by that event became nomadic, and the diaspora was eventually assimilated into a wide range of cultures that, themselves, were still spreading and mingling. Hence, it's a theory that there really WAS just one Great Flood, and everyone is just telling different versions of the same event. (Albeit one that occurred as a result of glacial recessions causing the flooding of a land below sea level and was far from global in scale.) See: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outburst_flood\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outburst_flood</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T19:54:32-08:00","id":422523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422507#post422507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, a theory of the global flood myth is that it occurred at an early enough period in time (basically, the last Ice Age) that the people who were displaced by that event became nomadic, and the diaspora was eventually assimilated into a wide range of cultures that, themselves, were still spreading and mingling. Hence, it's a theory that there really WAS just one Great Flood, and everyone is just telling different versions of the same event. (Albeit one that occurred as a result of glacial recessions causing the flooding of a land below sea level and was far from global in scale.) See: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outburst_flood\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outburst_flood</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it flooded the &quot;entire world&quot; in the sense that it flooded the area(s) where every basically every human being was living at the time, as I understand it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 02-27-2015, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T21:08:07-08:00","id":422583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422274#post422274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you think about it... maybe the various otherworlds are less the remains of Golden Roads than the fragments of the Golden Ladder? Or is there a difference? Maybe the Golden Ladder was a communal Golden Road erected by multiple Mages acting in concert?<br /> <br /> What happens if you take a five-pointed star, and fold the five arms so that their points touch?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://etc.usf.edu/clipart/43100/43188/pent1_43188_lg.gif\" target=\"_blank\">http://etc.usf.edu/clipart/43100/431...1_43188_lg.gif</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Also: In this headcanon, the God-Machine's job is to reassemble the Ladder by rejoining the five otherworlds. What has fallen must rise.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T01:02:19-08:00","id":422688,"title":"","content":"Well, there are several things from Xenu that I won't bother quoting all at once, but...<br /> <br /> I remember another thing out of Changeling that can conflict with the idea of Torpor being the Underworld, in that it's possible for Onieropomps to enter a dream in torpor. In fact, a Changeling can even end a torpid nightmare early and wake the vampire up, if they work at it, which mitigates some of the negative effects of torpor. That said, I'm not really into Vampire, nor have I read Geist, so there's some definite holes in my knowledge, there. <br /> <br /> In any event, my point in talking about finding the watchtower in Arcadia wasn't that Changeling Arcadia was absolutely the same thing as Supernal Arcadia, but that there was linkage between the cosmological game realms, even if only as a vestigial shadow or outright corruption of a severed portion of the Supernal. Your own &quot;overgrown golden road&quot; idea isn't terribly different from that. Rather, more of what I was going for was that there could be a sort of linkage of different games using their different viewpoints on the cosmos as sort of individual pieces on the same big jigsaw puzzle of the mystery of metaphysics in the nWoD.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, trying to say that one gameline is &quot;less canon&quot; than another, especially while trying to use Geist, another non-core, as part of the argument why is <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/SugarWiki/FictionIdentityPostulate\" target=\"_blank\">rather flimsy</a>. Apparently, all our crackpot theories are going to be retconned away as 2e sweeps through, anyway, but I'll stick with the ideas I like most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T01:33:11-08:00","id":422705,"title":"","content":"<i>Looks at the title.</i><br /> <br /> The Fall of Magi is in the same category as the Fall of the Uratha. Which both are mythical events which may have happened or haven't.<br /> <br /> Fall of Mage could've happened at the dawn of human evolution while the Uratha may have fell while the Shan'iatu were busy hiding out in the desert.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the AKD (The Hunter Org which is a link here), I've view them starting off as a family/friends of Magi who never awakened but remained on the islands as lore keepers, workers, and archivists. They were never powerful enough to be declared an Order but they were there. The Fall happened and they were scattered to the winds. Some where along the line, wolf blooded got included in the membership so when they reformed, the story changed to reflect two entirely different Falls into one and put the blame on both. Mission statement got hammered out, stories merged and retold, and the modern AKD was born.<br /> <br /> Never did liked how AKD nor Charon's history was set and I've had to revise both.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T10:19:23-08:00","id":423087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422688#post422688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there are several things from Xenu that I won't bother quoting all at once, but...<br /> <br /> I remember another thing out of Changeling that can conflict with the idea of Torpor being the Underworld, in that it's possible for Onieropomps to enter a dream in torpor. In fact, a Changeling can even end a torpid nightmare early and wake the vampire up, if they work at it, which mitigates some of the negative effects of torpor. That said, I'm not really into Vampire, nor have I read Geist, so there's some definite holes in my knowledge, there.<br /> <br /> In any event, my point in talking about finding the watchtower in Arcadia wasn't that Changeling Arcadia was absolutely the same thing as Supernal Arcadia, but that there was linkage between the cosmological game realms, even if only as a vestigial shadow or outright corruption of a severed portion of the Supernal. Your own &quot;overgrown golden road&quot; idea isn't terribly different from that. Rather, more of what I was going for was that there could be a sort of linkage of different games using their different viewpoints on the cosmos as sort of individual pieces on the same big jigsaw puzzle of the mystery of metaphysics in the nWoD.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, trying to say that one gameline is &quot;less canon&quot; than another, especially while trying to use Geist, another non-core, as part of the argument why is <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/SugarWiki/FictionIdentityPostulate\" target=\"_blank\">rather flimsy</a>. Apparently, all our crackpot theories are going to be retconned away as 2e sweeps through, anyway, but I'll stick with the ideas I like most.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not that one gameline is less canon, it's that the gameline rule books are canon and the expansion books aren't, as I understand it. So Inferno, for instance, is more of a grab bag of ideas whereas the WoD, Vampire, Mage, Werewolf, Changeling, Promethean, Geist, Mummy, Demon, and upcoming Beast corebooks are all canon. But then I don't actually play the games so much as I enjoy occasionally reading the books and creating headcanon, so I'm not really all that in the loop.<br /> <br /> I do agree with your implied sentiment that we shouldn't be looking for a Grand Unified Theory of the WoD Cosmology so much as exploring possibilities though; a big part of what makes it fun is the dynamic aspect of it. Once you go all Lord Business and attempt to Kragle everything in place it loses that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 02-28-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T10:28:50-08:00","id":423091,"title":"","content":"There really isn't one single canon. Even primary game line books can be seen as collections of ideas and suggestions. What ever you like from them is canon for your games, and what ever you don't like is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T11:13:28-08:00","id":423125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=423087#post423087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that one gameline is less canon, it's that the gameline rule books are canon and the expansion books aren't, as I understand it. So Inferno, for instance, is more of a grab bag of ideas whereas the WoD, Vampire, Mage, Werewolf, Changeling, Promethean, Geist, Mummy, Demon, and upcoming Beast corebooks are all canon. But then I don't actually play the games so much as I enjoy occasionally reading the books and creating headcanon, so I'm not really all that in the loop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if that's exactly true. The main three core books were created without further ideas fully fleshed out. That's why Mage is having to undergo tweaks so Atlantis and the Supernal are different. And in Werewolf's second edition, Father Wolf might not be a Father after all, plus Helios is getting more explained and we're really getting more information on the Shadow and Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:01:06-08:00","id":423340,"title":"","content":"It's also important to remember &quot;canon&quot; is not necessarily the most important thing to those writing the books. This is doubly true in New WoD which has a very toolkit approach to games.What is canon is far less important than giving options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:18:35-08:00","id":423489,"title":"","content":"What are the chances that Duat is connected to Pandemonium? I'm not too familiar with Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:51:13-08:00","id":423512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=423489#post423489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the chances that Duat is connected to Pandemonium? I'm not too familiar with Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Zero. It lies in the... other... direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:54:50-08:00","id":423513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=423512#post423512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Zero. It lies in the... other... direction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Towards the Inferno, away from the Supernal? Interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T16:01:01-08:00","id":423516,"title":"","content":"There's a Cosmology of the World of Darkness thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness\">here</a>, they've established that it is in the Lower Depths along with a lot of other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T20:24:33-08:00","id":423743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421538#post421538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nah. Second edition, they're not the same place. For reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I stand corrected. I'll puzzle this out when I have real time to think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T21:04:13-08:00","id":423801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421538#post421538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nah. Second edition, they're not the same place. For reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But are the CFae still maybe possibly the Old Gods of Thistle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T21:32:57-08:00","id":423811,"title":"","content":"I dunno, my working assumption has been that the Old Gods of the Thistle and the CFae are the same, but the Old Gods inhabit a Emanation Realm, and not the Supernal <i>per se</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T02:27:51-08:00","id":423921,"title":"","content":"My theory is that Faerie is what happened when the Old Gods of the Thistle got chucked out of the Supernal. It's not a realm, it's just a bunch of True Fae stacked on top of one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T08:16:44-08:00","id":424173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=423921#post423921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My theory is that Faerie is what happened when the Old Gods of the Thistle got chucked out of the Supernal. It's not a realm, it's just a bunch of True Fae stacked on top of one another.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But thanks to Fate/Time shenanigans, they both ARE and AREN'T still IN the Supernal proper.<br /> <br /> Goddamn True Fae and their mindbending metatime fuckery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:40:16-08:00","id":424437,"title":"","content":"Yea I was wondering if Duat was in the Lower Depths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:51:59-08:00","id":424445,"title":"","content":"It's in the Lower Depths as much as it can be, really. In the fact that mages label anything that takes something from the normal universe that it doesn't have. Seemingly, it doesn't have Sekhem, so... it steals. Ergo, a Lower Depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:00:04-08:00","id":424476,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Lower Depths&quot; is just a mage phrase that's better translated as &quot;Someplace strange that's out there somewhere.&quot; Basically, if you're not populated by the fae, astral projections, ghosts, angels, or spirits, then its &quot;lower depths.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mages are very good at trying to draw their world according to various models that are completely wrong. Which makes sense, really. They're a bunch of scientists trying to draw models of the world, but haven't quite realized that the Earth isn't the center of the universe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:12:03-08:00","id":424492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424445#post424445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in the Lower Depths as much as it can be, really. In the fact that mages label anything that takes something from the normal universe that it doesn't have. Seemingly, it doesn't have Sekhem, so... it steals. Ergo, a Lower Depth.</div> </div> </div> </div>What IS Sekhem, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:19:42-08:00","id":424505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424492#post424492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What IS Sekhem, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Life Force.<br /> Probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:22:29-08:00","id":424510,"title":"","content":"I tend to see the Lower Depths as somewhat darker and needful. I actually suspect the dead realm of the Helminth from Summoners is there rather than part of the Underworld proper. Summoners has the most intriguing stuff...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:52:01-08:00","id":424549,"title":"","content":"The overly simple version is 'life energy', but that's not quite accurate. It's more like 'vitality invested'. It's the life force/memory of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T15:08:16-08:00","id":424584,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think &quot;Life Energy&quot; sounds more like Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:24:50-08:00","id":424639,"title":"","content":"Interesting.<br /> <br /> There's a strong &quot;Old Gods cast out of the Supernal&quot; vibe to the Judges of Duat, isn't there? With Sekhem taking the place of the worship most Old Gods require.<br /> <br /> Then again, the CFae don't appear to require worship despite having been cast out of the Supernal (only they sorta kinda haven't, except they have, mostly, sometimes... I hate high-level Fate/Time magic...)<br /> <br /> And given the strong connection between symbols and the mind (whether it's the human mind or an inhuman one makes no nevermind) I can see a similar &quot;they've been thrown out but they kinda haven't&quot; vibe with the Judges. I mean, in the headcanon I'm brewing, they map to Mastigos/Pandemonium in the same way that the Old Gods of Thistle map to Acanthus/SArcadia.They've been expelled from the Supernal, but as Old Gods of Mind and Space, they maintain such a strong connection to the symbols that they're simultaneously in the Lower Depths and in an Emanation.<br /> <br /> Which is SCARY AS FUCK when you think about it.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they're not really in the Lower Depths at all. IIRC, nobody knows what happened to the Priests of Irem, right? What if they're Mages, who've Ascended? And maybe the Judges don't &quot;hunger&quot; for Sekhem so much as they're demanding it because it's a form of Quintessence that the Priests (obviously Alienated) can use for a Noumenon that restores the Judges to their rightful place...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:28:55-08:00","id":424642,"title":"","content":"The Fae eat conflict and stories. They even set up a system that allows them to sustain each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:45:53-08:00","id":424659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424639#post424639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting.<br /> <br /> There's a strong &quot;Old Gods cast out of the Supernal&quot; vibe to the Judges of Duat, isn't there? With Sekhem taking the place of the worship most Old Gods require.<br /> <br /> Then again, the CFae don't appear to require worship despite having been cast out of the Supernal (only they sorta kinda haven't, except they have, mostly, sometimes... I hate high-level Fate/Time magic...)<br /> <br /> And given the strong connection between symbols and the mind (whether it's the human mind or an inhuman one makes no nevermind) I can see a similar &quot;they've been thrown out but they kinda haven't&quot; vibe with the Judges. I mean, in the headcanon I'm brewing, they map to Mastigos/Pandemonium in the same way that the Old Gods of Thistle map to Acanthus/SArcadia.They've been expelled from the Supernal, but as Old Gods of Mind and Space, they maintain such a strong connection to the symbols that they're simultaneously in the Lower Depths and in an Emanation.<br /> <br /> Which is SCARY AS FUCK when you think about it.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they're not really in the Lower Depths at all. IIRC, nobody knows what happened to the Priests of Irem, right? What if they're Mages, who've Ascended? And maybe the Judges don't &quot;hunger&quot; for Sekhem so much as they're demanding it because it's a form of Quintessence that the Priests (obviously Alienated) can use for a Noumenon that restores the Judges to their rightful place...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you need to read the Book of the Deceived. It... complicates and changes a lot of the assumptions you're making, and provides a definitive explanation on what happened to at least 7 out of the 42 Shan'iatu.<br /> <br /> But most importantly, it makes me feel that Mind and Space may not be the most appropriate for the Judges. At least, not the Judges that the Shan'iatu first spoke to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:47:38-08:00","id":424660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424642#post424642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fae eat conflict and stories. They even set up a system that allows them to sustain each other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aha, so why aren't they lumped into the &quot;Lower Depths&quot; with the Judges then? Is it because the Judges actually remove Sekhmet from the world while the CFae/OGoT don't remove anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:53:30-08:00","id":424665,"title":"","content":"The True Fae remove people.<br /> <br /> But probably because people keep trying to make the Supernal Arcadia connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:04:47-08:00","id":424679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424659#post424659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you need to read the Book of the Deceived. It... complicates and changes a lot of the assumptions you're making, and provides a definitive explanation on what happened to at least 7 out of the 42 Shan'iatu.<br /> <br /> But most importantly, it makes me feel that Mind and Space may not be the most appropriate for the Judges. At least, not the Judges that the Shan'iatu first spoke to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll look into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:23:23-08:00","id":424691,"title":"","content":"I dunno if someone has mentioned it, but the best way to handle the World of Darkness is to <i>not</i> try and weave everything together. I mean, yeah, that defeats the entire &quot;infinite conspiracy&quot; that emerges, but the simple fact is that the nWoD argues with itself so wonderfully it's best to sit back and just let it go on its' own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:40:04-08:00","id":424698,"title":"","content":"Except these discussions are GREAT because, in some ways, they mirror the discussions the knowledgable have about their world. They are people too, and they will try and make them fit. It won't anymore than ours, but each and everyone of these discussions are enriching, even if they don't get 'anywhere'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:55:00-08:00","id":424714,"title":"","content":"The Supernal Realm of Aether is full of clockwork mechanisms and blazing angels... if you were running a Mage/Demon crossover game (which is one of my interests), it might be neat to have the Realm of Aether and the God-Machine linked, perhaps with the G-M and its angels as the Fallen World reflection of something in the Aether which has been turned to another use. But I wouldn't expect that to be supported in any of the canonical Mage stuff, or Demon stuff. Not to mention that the &quot;Aether&quot; Demons use isn't the primal creative force one might find in the Realm of Aether, but is the filtered byproduct of Angelic or God-Machine activity. Demonic Aether should really be called something else, but I guess the White Wolf thesaurus only stretches so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4832-dannyk","name":"DannyK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:13:38-08:00","id":424754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424698#post424698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except these discussions are GREAT because, in some ways, they mirror the discussions the knowledgable have about their world. They are people too, and they will try and make them fit. It won't anymore than ours, but each and everyone of these discussions are enriching, even if they don't get 'anywhere'.</div> </div> </div> </div>'snot about solving any mysteries, 'sabout generating ideas folks can use for stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:27:00-08:00","id":424755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424659#post424659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you need to read the Book of the Deceived. It... complicates and changes a lot of the assumptions you're making, and provides a definitive explanation on what happened to at least 7 out of the 42 Shan'iatu.<br /> <br /> But most importantly, it makes me feel that Mind and Space may not be the most appropriate for the Judges. At least, not the Judges that the Shan'iatu first spoke to.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Judges of Life vs. Judges of Death. The Shan'iatu (minus the Deceived) became the Judges of Death, who are the Judges of Duat. But with the Deceived being kicked out, that leaves only 35, so 7 more had to come from somewhere else.<br /> <br /> But we don't really know anything about the Judges of Life, do we?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:32:50-08:00","id":424760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424755#post424755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we don't really know anything about the Judges of Life, do we?</div> </div> </div> </div>We know that Azar was their voice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:49:23-08:00","id":424766,"title":"","content":"We don't even definitively know that the Judges of Duat aren't the Judges of Life. After all, it is mentioned that the Judges of Life descend to Duat to judge the souls of the living.<br /> <br /> Really, the only evidence about the Judges in the Mummy core being different from the Judges of Life is the argument &quot;Oh, some of the Judges look kinda messed up physically. That doesn't sound like something with the title 'of life'&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:55:45-08:00","id":424788,"title":"","content":"From the implications in Deceived. My guess is that the Judges of Duat are not the Judges of Life which felt fairly clear to me and that what they(The Judges of Duat) are in relation to the non 6th Guild Shan'iatu is....complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:58:41-08:00","id":424790,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, call me crazy if you like, because this opinion is pretty heretical to the Mage worldview- but the Supernal Realms are symbols made truer than true. Examples that are better than the thing they represent, or perfected ideas. If that's true, then what are they representing?<br /> <br /> My view is the Mages have it wrong. Gnostic worldview and all, they're a little biased. You can't have an example without a base. My perception is that the Supernal Realms are reflections of the rest of the World of Darkness, and not the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T20:01:41-08:00","id":424793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424766#post424766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't even definitively know that the Judges of Duat aren't the Judges of Life. After all, it is mentioned that the Judges of Life descend to Duat to judge the souls of the living.<br /> <br /> Really, the only evidence about the Judges in the Mummy core being different from the Judges of Life is the argument &quot;Oh, some of the Judges look kinda messed up physically. That doesn't sound like something with the title 'of life'&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Judges of Duat judge the dead, which was originally Anpu's job, yes? Then Azar kicked him out and demoted him to guardian of the Neter-khertet, and took over his old job. Once the Shan'iatu arrived (with their 7 new buddies, presumably), he delegated the judging to them.<br /> <br /> Of course, all this is assuming that Why the Stars Fall is mostly accurate, which isn't a particularly safe assumption, what with being in-game fiction presented by an unreliable narrator (he even admits that he lied twice deliberately and wonders how many times he lied to himself). We also don't have game stats for the author at the time of the writing, so we don't know how high his Memory was. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T20:02:00-08:00","id":424794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424790#post424790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so, call me crazy if you like, because this opinion is pretty heretical to the Mage worldview- [\u2026]You can't have an example without a base. My perception is that the Supernal Realms are reflections of the rest of the World of Darkness, and not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026I'm going to go ahead and take this as tacit admission that you haven't read Imperial Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T20:10:02-08:00","id":424799,"title":"","content":"I wonder, given the nature of that which is discussed in regards to Mummy, if spoilers might be appropriate.<br /> <br /> Probably not, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T20:20:02-08:00","id":424805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424799#post424799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, given the nature of that which is discussed in regards to Mummy, if spoilers might be appropriate.<br /> <br /> Probably not, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. If a mod wants to spoilerblock stuff, they can spoilerblock stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T20:44:51-08:00","id":424836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424790#post424790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so, call me crazy if you like, because this opinion is pretty heretical to the Mage worldview- but the Supernal Realms are symbols made truer than true. Examples that are better than the thing they represent, or perfected ideas. If that's true, then what are they representing?<br /> <br /> My view is the Mages have it wrong. Gnostic worldview and all, they're a little biased. You can't have an example without a base. My perception is that the Supernal Realms are reflections of the rest of the World of Darkness, and not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize, 1e Mage doesn't even work that way. It's been mentioned in a few places that based on what Mages are able to see, it's not completely clear that there is any such thing as The Supernal is only a reflection of the Fallen World/The Fallen World is a reflection, distillation, etc of the Platonisms of the Supernatural world. Some suspect it's a mix but they are unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T21:43:45-08:00","id":424883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424836#post424836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You realize, 1e Mage doesn't even work that way. It's been mentioned in a few places that based on what Mages are able to see, it's not completely clear that there is any such thing as The Supernal is only a reflection of the Fallen World/The Fallen World is a reflection, distillation, etc of the Platonisms of the Supernatural world. Some suspect it's a mix but they are unclear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's pretty much a chicken/egg thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T23:28:01-08:00","id":424914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424805#post424805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meh. If a mod wants to spoilerblock stuff, they can spoilerblock stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really not our job. If you want to put spoiler tags on stuff, you can. If you don't, it's not against any rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T04:16:52-08:00","id":425003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424793#post424793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the Judges of Duat judge the dead, which was originally Anpu's job, yes? Then Azar kicked him out and demoted him to guardian of the Neter-khertet, and took over his old job. Once the Shan'iatu arrived (with their 7 new buddies, presumably), he delegated the judging to them.<br /> <br /> Of course, all this is assuming that Why the Stars Fall is mostly accurate, which isn't a particularly safe assumption, what with being in-game fiction presented by an unreliable narrator (he even admits that he lied twice deliberately and wonders how many times he lied to himself). We also don't have game stats for the author at the time of the writing, so we don't know how high his Memory was. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;And the Judges had given the Remet five powers, to guide them to a place called Duat, to appear before the 42 for a final destiny in accordance with their obedience to the Law.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Judging was not Anpu's job. Nor is it Azar's.<br /> <br /> That said, yeah, the story itself hardly offers a complete picture, but it isn't hard to make the argument that the 42 beings that once existed still exist in the same roles, as opposed to claiming that 35 other beings became 42 and imposed themselves on reality. The only other explanation to hand is that the process created a second set of 42 beings from whole cloth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T05:33:46-08:00","id":425036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424794#post424794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026I'm going to go ahead and take this as tacit admission that you haven't read Imperial Mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in a very, very long time. And it was more of a skim the first time through. It's been a while since I've gotten into mage, so chances are I shoved my foot very far into my mouth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424836#post424836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You realize, 1e Mage doesn't even work that way. It's been mentioned in a few places that based on what Mages are able to see, it's not completely clear that there is any such thing as The Supernal is only a reflection of the Fallen World/The Fallen World is a reflection, distillation, etc of the Platonisms of the Supernatural world. Some suspect it's a mix but they are unclear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto to this. Haven't really read a lot of the mage stuff in a very long time- should probably have started with that. In which case, I apologize for intruding on intelligent conversation with opinions based on badly-remembered lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 03-02-2015, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T06:29:38-08:00","id":425104,"title":"","content":"No need to. Is true that IM points out that the Supernal needs the Phenomenal to give it meaning as much as the Phenomenal needs the Supernal to give it concept. Also, it seems one of the key defining differences between the three big blocks of Mage society in second edition (the Diamond Orders, the Council of Free Asemblies and the Seers of the Throne) is how they see the Supernal-Phenomenal realtionship.<br /> <br /> The Free Council is the one that sees the &quot;Fallen&quot; world influencing back the Supernal as much as the second influences the first if I remeber the drafts right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T06:58:05-08:00","id":425123,"title":"","content":"So why isn't the Shadow considered a Lower Depth? It requires presence from the material world.<br /> <br /> Or the material world, for that matter, if it requires Supernal influence? Or does Lower Depths classification necessitate needing something from the material world, no matter that ones state?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-02-2015, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T07:01:56-08:00","id":425129,"title":"","content":"Because the shadow covers an entire arcarnum the material is naturally lacking, and the material gets as much from it as it does from the material. They are two parts of the same realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:27:09-08:00","id":425297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425003#post425003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&amp;quot;And the Judges had given the Remet five powers, to guide them to a place called Duat, to appear before the 42 for a final destiny in accordance with their obedience to the Law.&amp;quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Judging was not Anpu's job. Nor is it Azar's.<br /> <br /> That said, yeah, the story itself hardly offers a complete picture, but it isn't hard to make the argument that the 42 beings that once existed still exist in the same roles, as opposed to claiming that 35 other beings became 42 and imposed themselves on reality. The only other explanation to hand is that the process created a second set of 42 beings from whole cloth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. So if the Judges of Life were and still are the Judges of Duat, then what exactly are Azar and the Shan'iatu doing? Just chillin' in the afterlife? Kickin' back with some beer and dead bitches? They sought to become Judges of Death with Azar as their King, and they sent Irem to the Afterlife; maybe the idea is that they set up their empire in the eternal realm of Death and rather than judging the recently departed for their crimes in life, they rule over those who have escaped Ammut and passed into eternity.<br /> <br /> That seems to match up with the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-02-2015, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:23:37-08:00","id":425443,"title":"","content":"Yea the Shadow, like the Underworld, is very intrinsically linked to the physical world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:11:00-08:00","id":425527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425129#post425129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the shadow covers an entire arcarnum the material is naturally lacking, and the material gets as much from it as it does from the material. They are two parts of the same realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems somewhat arbitrary on the part of the Mages IMO. There's a rather strong argument to be made that the Inferno is a Realm Invisible rather than a Lower Depth, yet because the material isn't lacking in Mind, the Inferno gets relegated to Here be Dragons status even though its residents don't appear to be REMOVING anything from the material, IIRC, so much as encouraging the GENERATION of Vice that they can feed on, much as the the CFae generate conflict and stories to eat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:39:37-08:00","id":425544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425527#post425527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems somewhat arbitrary on the part of the Mages IMO. There's a rather strong argument to be made that the Inferno is a Realm Invisible rather than a Lower Depth, yet because the material isn't lacking in Mind, the Inferno gets relegated to Here be Dragons status even though its residents don't appear to be REMOVING anything from the material, IIRC, so much as encouraging the GENERATION of Vice that they can feed on, much as the the CFae generate conflict and stories to eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>All scientific models are founded on assumptions. Those assumptions are usually not correct, at least not entirely, and when new discoveries cause the scientists to question those assumptions, the process of developing new hypothesies begins. However, a new model must either explain more, or explain the same amount in a simpler way. The model the Awakened currently use to explain the various realms and their relationships is imperfect, and I imagine most Awakened scholars are keenly aware of that fact, but it is <i>thus far</i> the most complete and efficient one they have. There are presumably some who hypothesize the Inferno may be something other than a Lower Depth, but lack sufficient empirical data to form a new model that incorporates that assumption <i>and</i> is more complete or simpler than the standard model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:43:58-08:00","id":425548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425544#post425544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All scientific models are founded on assumptions. Those assumptions are usually not correct, at least not entirely, and when new discoveries cause the scientists to question those assumptions, the process of developing new hypothesies begins. However, a new model must either explain more, or explain the same amount in a simpler way. The model the Awakened currently use to explain the various realms and their relationships is imperfect, and I imagine most Awakened scholars are keenly aware of that fact, but it is <i>thus far</i> the most complete and efficient one they have. There are presumably some who hypothesize the Inferno may be something other than a Lower Depth, but lack sufficient empirical data to form a new model that incorporates that assumption <i>and</i> is more complete or simpler than the standard model.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey, Hermes, you wanna come with me and gather some empirical data on the Inferno?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Fuck you, Pythagoras, I like being alive. You can go get YOUR soul eaten, leave me out of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Actually, I'm working on a new theory, I don't think Infernals eat sou-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Fuck. You.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-02-2015, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:02:42-08:00","id":425581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425548#post425548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Hey, Hermes, you wanna come with me and gather some empirical data on the Inferno?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Fuck you, Pythagoras, I like being alive. You can go get YOUR soul eaten, leave me out of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Actually, I'm working on a new theory, I don't think Infernals eat sou-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Fuck. You.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Pythagoras disappears for a year, then shows up again as a Qliphoth. The other Mages in his Consilium hold this up as evidence that the Inferno is actually connected to the Abyss somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:08:41-08:00","id":425591,"title":"","content":"You know, it occurs to me, apropo of nothing, that the fact that the Shan'iatu may be the entire reason the World of Darkness is as screwed up as it is. We have no clear idea what's going on with the real shadows of the Law, but the Temakh Judges may still be at war with them, or may of polluted the fundamental beginnings of everything, creating a cascade of breaking reality that's only stopped by every other screwed up thing that was born from their shitting around saying &quot;Nope, we're keeping creation.&quot; <br /> <br /> This, of course, works on a lot of assumptions, like ignoring the impact and involvement of spirits and ghosts on creation, or the fact that I reckon the Supernal to be younger than the Mummy cosmology, the spirits cosmology, and the ghosts cosmology, as well as a few other things (Pretty much everything <i>but</i> mage cosmology, and possibly Promethean's as well).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:47:21-08:00","id":425636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425591#post425591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, it occurs to me, apropo of nothing, that the fact that the Shan'iatu may be the entire reason the World of Darkness is as screwed up as it is. We have no clear idea what's going on with the real shadows of the Law, but the Temakh Judges may still be at war with them, or may of polluted the fundamental beginnings of everything, creating a cascade of breaking reality that's only stopped by every other screwed up thing that was born from their shitting around saying &quot;Nope, we're keeping creation.&quot;<br /> <br /> This, of course, works on a lot of assumptions, like ignoring the impact and involvement of spirits and ghosts on creation, or the fact that I reckon the Supernal to be younger than the Mummy cosmology, the spirits cosmology, and the ghosts cosmology, as well as a few other things (Pretty much everything <i>but</i> mage cosmology, and possibly Promethean's as well).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the current universe is probably an amalgamation of multiple timelines, so that may be why things are fucked up in ONE version of reality.<br /> <br /> Whether it's the &quot;oldest&quot; version of reality in terms of metatime, or whether the others are the same &quot;age&quot; and they all kind of melded together at the point of their respective catastrophes, or if you have, say, 3 realities that are &quot;older&quot; than the rest, or some other possibility, is entirely too brain-breaking to puzzle out as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> I kinda envision, though, that all the timelines have one major feature in common: Humanity, or a close relation thereto, fucked everything up.<br /> <br /> We delved too greedily, and too deep, and we broke the universe in some fundamental manner. Found a loose thread in the tapestry and tugged on it, finding to our horror that it unraveled the whole thing.<br /> <br /> The current world is the result of a clumsy splice of the frayed threads of the previous, broken ones, joined together at the point of their respective Falls. The Realms Invisible are the bits where outlying parts of the different tapestries are joined imperfectly and overlap, their threads interweaving with one another; the border realms (Hedge, Twilight, Autochthonous Depths, et al) are the seams where new thread's been stitched in to prevent the haphazard mess from coming apart again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:47:10-08:00","id":425766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=424691#post424691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno if someone has mentioned it, but the best way to handle the World of Darkness is to <i>not</i> try and weave everything together. I mean, yeah, that defeats the entire &quot;infinite conspiracy&quot; that emerges, but the simple fact is that the nWoD argues with itself so wonderfully it's best to sit back and just let it go on its' own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is more interesting?<br /> <br /> A story where there is a coherent narrative, heroes and villains working towards their own respective purposes, and a climax and conclusion that matches the themes of the story and where the audience is built up in anticipation for this conclusion...<br /> <br /> ... Or a story with completely random actors popping up out of nowhere, unannounced, full of sound and fury, signifying nothing, that involves nothing so much as a bunch of unintelligible STUFF happening with no rhyme, meaning, plot, climax, or resolution?<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is, at its core, a mystery. At least, a whole bundle of mysteries. Now, there are some multiple-choice cosmologies at play, here, by design, but it's set up specifically to invite the player to try to find ways that all the puzzle pieces CAN fit together. And besides, if, when you hear something go bump in the night, and you decide it's probably just some alley cat, not worth looking into what are you even doing in the World of Darkness as a protagonist, anyway? It's that desire to know that is the core motivation of the story. The reveal is what you paid the price of admission to see. You wouldn't be satisfied with a game that has the major players never get revealed, none of the events resolved, just shuffling your characters off to the next bright flashy thing before you figured out what happened in the last bright flashy thing, or ever stopping a villain or monster, would you?<br /> <br /> These exercises are another part of that core mystery-solving experience that are the hook of WoD. It seems like telling people to just stop having fun to tell them that they're not allowed to explore the game world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:07:35-08:00","id":425799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425766#post425766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A story where there is a coherent narrative, heroes and villains working towards their own respective purposes, and a climax and conclusion that matches the themes of the story and where the audience is built up in anticipation for this conclusion...<br /> <br /> ... Or a story with completely random actors popping up out of nowhere, unannounced, full of sound and fury, signifying nothing, that involves nothing so much as a bunch of unintelligible STUFF happening with no rhyme, meaning, plot, climax, or resolution?</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot in good conscience let this stand as a purportedly legitimate argument.<br /> <br /> The cosmology of the World of Darkness on the scale people are talking about is beyond the scope of anything outside an individual game to address and (please note that I say this as someone who's been a nWoD cosmology buff for pretty much as long as I've been a nWoD fan) <i>completely irrelevant</i> to the day-to-day stories-about-humanity that the gamelines tend to be direct neighbors to. That's kind of the <i>point</i> \u2014 the mechanisms of the occult go farther from relatable human experience the deeper you go, and, as the point of &quot;mages are monsters&quot; illustrates, developing prime familiarity with them tends to have the opportunity cost of dealing with people as people instead of parts.<br /> <br /> It's a fun diversion, but the fact of the matter is that\u2026 well\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Winter Masques, p103, &quot;Endless Faces&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The world\u2019s cultures and mythologies are a thousand layers deep. Digging into them reveals new things every time: bloated demons filled with wind, beautiful women cobbled together from blood and sea-foam, thunder-throwing gods who temper their anger with lust and jealousy.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is not, in fact, a definite end to &quot;the whole cosmology,&quot; not least because it's changing all the time due to confounding variables half the supernatural population hadn't even conceived of. It's almost literally a Sisyphean task, except the hill gets taller after every summit and pieces of the boulder keep breaking off whose usefulness is nigh-impossible to verify and also you don't have the dubious benefit of being already dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:49:23-08:00","id":425865,"title":"","content":"I love how every nWoD cosmology conversation inevitably generates all these high-concept metaphors packed with evocative language and just short of making any actual sense. I'm not being facetious, I genuinely enjoy all the purple prose that comes out of these talks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:51:10-08:00","id":425868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425766#post425766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is more interesting?<br /> <br /> A story where there is a coherent narrative, heroes and villains working towards their own respective purposes, and a climax and conclusion that matches the themes of the story and where the audience is built up in anticipation for this conclusion...<br /> <br /> ... Or a story with completely random actors popping up out of nowhere, unannounced, full of sound and fury, signifying nothing, that involves nothing so much as a bunch of unintelligible STUFF happening with no rhyme, meaning, plot, climax, or resolution?<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is, at its core, a mystery. At least, a whole bundle of mysteries. Now, there are some multiple-choice cosmologies at play, here, by design, but it's set up specifically to invite the player to try to find ways that all the puzzle pieces CAN fit together. And besides, if, when you hear something go bump in the night, and you decide it's probably just some alley cat, not worth looking into what are you even doing in the World of Darkness as a protagonist, anyway? It's that desire to know that is the core motivation of the story. The reveal is what you paid the price of admission to see. You wouldn't be satisfied with a game that has the major players never get revealed, none of the events resolved, just shuffling your characters off to the next bright flashy thing before you figured out what happened in the last bright flashy thing, or ever stopping a villain or monster, would you?<br /> <br /> These exercises are another part of that core mystery-solving experience that are the hook of WoD. It seems like telling people to just stop having fun to tell them that they're not allowed to explore the game world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And this right here is why the final episodes of Battlestar Galactica, Lost, and The X-Files all blew.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425799#post425799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot in good conscience let this stand as a purportedly legitimate argument.<br /> <br /> The cosmology of the World of Darkness on the scale people are talking about is beyond the scope of anything outside an individual game to address and (please note that I say this as someone who's been a nWoD cosmology buff for pretty much as long as I've been a nWoD fan) <i>completely irrelevant</i> to the day-to-day stories-about-humanity that the gamelines tend to be direct neighbors to. That's kind of the <i>point</i> \u2014 the mechanisms of the occult go farther from relatable human experience the deeper you go, and, as the point of &quot;mages are monsters&quot; illustrates, developing prime familiarity with them tends to have the opportunity cost of dealing with people as people instead of parts.<br /> <br /> It's a fun diversion, but the fact of the matter is that\u2026 well\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is not, in fact, a definite end to &quot;the whole cosmology,&quot; not least because it's changing all the time due to confounding variables half the supernatural population hadn't even conceived of. It's almost literally a Sisyphean task, except the hill gets taller after every summit and pieces of the boulder keep breaking off whose usefulness is nigh-impossible to verify and also you don't have the dubious benefit of being already dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the boulder <b>BITES</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:02:43-08:00","id":425873,"title":"","content":"In defense of Lost, they had a plan for a much more cohesive story. Then the guy who came up with the plan left without telling anyone how it was supposed to end. Then two of the actors whose characters were both intricately tied into the plot they put together to try to salvage the show left. Then the network told them the cash cow had run out of milk and they had one season to end the show. There was no way ther were going to come up with a satisfying conclusion to the plot AND resolve all of the characters' backstories. Given that the show was really always more about the characters than the mysteries (which had already been perceived as a joke by the fan base since like season 3 anyway), they opted to resolve the backstories rather than the plot. Honestly, I think they made the best they could have made out of all the shit that was heaped on them. It ended up a show that was good not for the actual story it told, but for the way they told it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:22:22-08:00","id":425934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425873#post425873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In defense of Lost, they had a plan for a much more cohesive story. Then the guy who came up with the plan left without telling anyone how it was supposed to end. Then two of the actors whose characters were both intricately tied into the plot they put together to try to salvage the show left. Then the network told them the cash cow had run out of milk and they had one season to end the show. There was no way ther were going to come up with a satisfying conclusion to the plot AND resolve all of the characters' backstories. Given that the show was really always more about the characters than the mysteries (which had already been perceived as a joke by the fan base since like season 3 anyway), they opted to resolve the backstories rather than the plot. Honestly, I think they made the best they could have made out of all the shit that was heaped on them. It ended up a show that was good not for the actual story it told, but for the way they told it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why you ALWAYS create a writer's bible before you start production!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:34:53-08:00","id":425943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425868#post425868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this right here is why the final episodes of Battlestar Galactica, Lost, and The X-Files all blew.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never watched any of those three shows, honestly. Any show that puffs itself up so much upon &quot;DRAMA&quot; because they rely upon &quot;shocking episodes&quot; to boost ratings rather than actually trying to make any sort of sense is inevitably going to lead to such an obvious let-down.<br /> <br /> Further, they're just flat unenjoyable even before the conclusions, because you know they aren't capable of pulling it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 03-02-2015, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:35:27-08:00","id":425944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425799#post425799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a fun diversion, but the fact of the matter is that\u2026 well\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why, exactly, are you trying to ruin everyone's fun?<br /> <br /> The point of the game, again, is to explore the mystery. Because exploring the mystery is fun. <br /> <br /> Now, maybe you're not interested in seeing an overarching storyline to the whole thing, but to take a stance that it's wrong to want to mentally explore is a stance that runs across the grain of many people's personalities. Further, it's honestly just not terribly respectable. It's holding up intellectual laziness as a virtue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:47:28-08:00","id":426007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425944#post425944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of the game, again, is to explore the mystery. Because exploring the mystery is fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of the game is to tell a story that includes &quot;explore the mystery without getting devoured by it.&quot; Kindly refrain from calling me an intellectually lazy fun-ruiner for agreeing that this is a game that deals with personlike characters and explicitly lacks definite answers to questions of fundamental cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:50:51-08:00","id":426013,"title":"","content":"It really would be nice if mythology, culture and the weird all made sense and fit into neat categories. But they don't in real life, nevermind the extreme weirdness and mystery of the World of Darkness. I don't really see the need to fit it all into neat little boxes, since life has never worked like that, and it honestly makes things more interesting. It feels like a bad habit from DnD games and the like, where gods have really clear purviews and they come up with an exacting cosmic order and all that.<br /> <br /> I think people tend to mistake this sort of approach for being lazy, which I really don't think is fair. I'm sure someone better versed in the books could give you the lowdown, but wherever metaphysics are discussed in the books, even when there isn't a direct connection made, there seem to be underlying ideas that recur in places. One thing that comes to mind is how the True Fae and Archmasters, as really high level templates, seem to have similar schticks going on in comparison with one another, with stuff like Ochemata and Actors and Royal Avatars for high ranking spirits. I think Dave mentioned somewhere the idea that these kinds of high ranking creatures are both character and setting, or something like that.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of little stuff that's consistent like that, and if you're looking for &quot;unified cosmology&quot; spotting those patterns is probably gonna be the best thing you'll get/the most rewarding stuff to look out for.<br /> <br /> Lastly, whether you're playing a game of Vampire or Changeling or whatever, this kind of stuff doesn't actually come up all that often, though grasping the edges of mysteries can be part of the fun (Think stuff like the Strix's claims of being the Beast, and whether it's really legit or not.) Even in Mage, where some people expect that they should have all the answers, it's the Mystery that is central to the experience, not the chart of all mysticism ever. In fact, one might even argue that a big part of what makes a Mage game interesting is where their metaphysical models fail to really map out phenomena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-02-2015, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:57:19-08:00","id":426021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425944#post425944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then why, exactly, are you trying to ruin everyone's fun?<br /> <br /> The point of the game, again, is to explore the mystery. Because exploring the mystery is fun.<br /> <br /> Now, maybe you're not interested in seeing an overarching storyline to the whole thing, but to take a stance that it's wrong to want to mentally explore is a stance that runs across the grain of many people's personalities. Further, it's honestly just not terribly respectable. It's holding up intellectual laziness as a virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what he was getting at was that basically, no individual game would conceivably need a cohesive, overarching cosmology. However, this fails to account for three facts:<br /> <br /> 1. Imperial Mysteries is a thing.<br /> 2. Crossover games are a thing.<br /> 3. Players love cohesive, overarching cosmologies.<br /> <br /> The natural result of 1, 2, and 3 is that someone is going to run a crossover game with the Ascension War as its backdrop, and the PCs, drawn from amongst multiple splats, acting as pawns/servants/go-betweens in the machinations of the Archmasters/Old Gods/etc.<br /> <br /> So what happens when a Deceived Mummy enters the Inferno, starts throwing around Utterances with the aid of an Astra, and his target is a God-Machine Demon whose Cover is a former Promethean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:03:52-08:00","id":426031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=426021#post426021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think what he was getting at was that basically, no individual game would conceivably need a cohesive, overarching cosmology. However, this fails to account for three facts:<br /> <br /> 1. Imperial Mysteries is a thing.<br /> 2. Crossover games are a thing.<br /> 3. Players love cohesive, overarching cosmologies.<br /> <br /> The natural result of 1, 2, and 3 is that someone is going to run a crossover game with the Ascension War as its backdrop, and the PCs, drawn from amongst multiple splats, acting as pawns/servants/go-betweens in the machinations of the Archmasters/Old Gods/etc.<br /> <br /> So what happens when a Deceived Mummy enters the Inferno, starts throwing around Utterances with the aid of an Astra, and his target is a God-Machine Demon whose Cover is a former Promethean?</div> </div> </div> </div>None of these except for 3 need cosmology answers, and your last question is a question of mechanics. If you're playing the game in these parameters, you've already gone beyond the scope of the books. You have all the pieces to put your setting together, that's what the New World of Darkness is meant to do. Good luck trying to fit it all into neat little boxes.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Inferno accounts for splats prior to Mummy's release, and Demon accounts for a Demon who tried to nab a Cover from another supernatural being. So it doesn't explicitly outline the above scenario, but it does address most of the variables of that situation. The games won't ever likely address whatever highly exacting scenario you can come up with, but most up to date books like Book of the Dead or Inferno account for those groups at their time of release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-02-2015, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:04:19-08:00","id":426032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=426021#post426021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what he was getting at was that basically, no individual game would conceivably need a cohesive, overarching cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So what happens when a Deceived Mummy enters the Inferno, starts throwing around Utterances with the aid of an Astra, and his target is a God-Machine Demon whose Cover is a former Promethean? </div> </div> </div>In general: that sounds like a fantastic question to answer <i>in the game in which it is happening</i>, because that degree of involvement is too contrived to really merit addressing in the books to the degree that there would be sufficient precedent to draw from.<br /> <br /> As regards this example in particular, though:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">We already went off the rails when you brought one of the Deceived to another dimension, because the Sixth Guild can't depart from the material realm.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:09:31-08:00","id":426043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=426031#post426031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None of these except for 3 need cosmology answers, and your last question is a question of mechanics. If you're playing the game in these parameters, you've already gone beyond the scope of the books. You have all the pieces to put your setting together, that's what the New World of Darkness is meant to do. Good luck trying to fit it all into neat little boxes.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Inferno accounts for splats prior to Mummy's release, and Demon accounts for a Demon who tried to nab a Cover from another supernatural being. So it doesn't explicitly outline the above scenario, but it does address most of the variables of that situation. The games won't ever likely address whatever highly exacting scenario you can come up with, but most up to date books like Book of the Dead or Inferno account for those groups at their time of release.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and going beyond the scope of the books is exactly what these cosmology-building exercises are about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=426032#post426032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> In general: that sounds like a fantastic question to answer <i>in the game in which it is happening</i>, because that degree of involvement is too contrived to really merit addressing in the books to the degree that there would be sufficient precedent to draw from.<br /> <br /> As regards this example in particular, though:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">We already went off the rails when you brought one of the Deceived to another dimension, because the Sixth Guild can't depart from the material realm.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Which is exactly why the Storyteller would need to come up with a cosmology (which would inform the mechanical aspects); unless you're heavily railroading your players, this kind of thing could come up pretty easily without a lot of advance warning.<br /> <br /> 2. People can't come back from the dead either, but Mages can <b>make</b> it happen, let alone Archmasters. But we can sub in a Sin-Eater instead, or a regular Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-02-2015, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:19:29-08:00","id":426047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=426043#post426043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Which is exactly why the Storyteller would need to come up with a cosmology (which would inform the mechanical aspects); unless you're heavily railroading your players, this kind of thing could come up pretty easily without a lot of advance warning.</div> </div> </div> </div>*sigh* Where's that old Omicron post\u2026 ah, here we are:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't you know that continuity errors are an integral part of pulp fantasy, and that <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default1eb6.html?g=posts&amp;m=1692992#post1692992\" target=\"_blank\">half the fun of it is in forcing fans years down the line to piece together fragments that do not fit the supposed continuity of your narrative, which they imagine as written with care and attention by a dedicated author</a> when in fact you half-assed it at 3 in the morning while drunk on whiskeys because Weird Tales needs your short story for yesterday and who is that Ulgumoz already? dammit let's say he's a wizard and be done with it </div> </div> </div>No plan survives contact with the players and that goes double for maps of the magic(k)al cosmos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-02-2015, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:35:23-08:00","id":426056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=426047#post426047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*sigh* Where's that old Omicron post\u2026 ah, here we are:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No plan survives contact with the players and that goes double for maps of the magic(k)al cosmos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, except in this case the authors are deliberately trolling us by going out of their way to debunk our headcanon. And then we turn around and revise the headcanon to incorporate the new info and come up with something EVEN COOLER.<br /> <br /> It's like a beautiful dance, except a bunch of fictional people get their souls eaten and go insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:53:54-08:00","id":426068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=426056#post426056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, except in this case the authors are deliberately trolling us by going out of their way to debunk our headcanon. And then we turn around and revise the headcanon to incorporate the new info and come up with something EVEN COOLER.</div> </div> </div> </div>I struggle to imagine the Paradise you must live in where the authors are producing new material at a clip capable of matching the pace of your average game, much less why you believe the authors' continued involvement is necessary to the practical application of this process.<br /> <br /> The laws of the supernatural world are filled with exceptions and subject to change. The big picture isn't actually that interesting on its own, global-to-universal as it is, hence the focus in-game on scales where you can actually see the principal actors and those points of interface.<br /> <br /> I've pointed to Zelazny's <i>Chronicles of Amber</i> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/292603-the-cosmology-thread-forcing-square-pegs-into-other-square-pegs?p=310861#post310861\">before</a>, and seeing as that's a series where the protagonist at one point <i>literally sits down to tea with a manifestation of the principle of multiversal Order</i> I think it bears attention as a relevant example of how high-power games still need grounding; the cosmology is a variable curiosity \u2014 the people caught in the middle of it all are what the story's actually about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T20:02:30-08:00","id":426075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=426068#post426068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I struggle to imagine the Paradise you must live in where the authors are producing new material at a clip capable of matching the pace of your average game, much less why you believe the authors' continued involvement is necessary to the practical application of this process.<br /> <br /> The laws of the supernatural world are filled with exceptions and subject to change. The big picture isn't actually that interesting on its own, global-to-universal as it is, hence the focus in-game on scales where you can actually see the principal actors and those points of interface.<br /> <br /> I've pointed to Zelazny's <i>Chronicles of Amber</i> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/292603-the-cosmology-thread-forcing-square-pegs-into-other-square-pegs?p=310861#post310861\">before</a>, and seeing as that's a series where the protagonist at one point <i>literally sits down to tea with a manifestation of the principle of multiversal Order</i> I think it bears attention as a relevant example of how high-power games still need grounding; the cosmology is a variable curiosity \u2014 the people caught in the middle of it all are what the story's actually about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't actually play; this is all just a fascinating exercise in worldbuilding for me. But if I <i>did</i> play, I'd be the Storyteller in a sprawling, epic, universe-spanning Chronicle involving multiple groups who might or might not ever sit down at the same table together, and it'd last five years, minimum.<br /> <br /> Or, more likely, it'd implode when it turned out to be impossible to actually run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:22:38-08:00","id":426203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425766#post425766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is more interesting?<br /> <br /> A story where there is a coherent narrative, heroes and villains working towards their own respective purposes, and a climax and conclusion that matches the themes of the story and where the audience is built up in anticipation for this conclusion...<br /> <br /> ... Or a story with completely random actors popping up out of nowhere, unannounced, full of sound and fury, signifying nothing, that involves nothing so much as a bunch of unintelligible STUFF happening with no rhyme, meaning, plot, climax, or resolution?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) You've clearly never read <i>Strangeness in the Proportion</i>.<br /> <br /> 2) Stories don't happen on the scale we're discussing. Stories are people level. They can be about people doing things that pertain to these large scales, but in the end it's people stories are about.<br /> <br /> 3) I enjoy stories with coherent narrative, protagonists and antagonists working towards their own respective purposes, with a climax and conclusion that matches the themes of the story and where the audience receives catharsis from anticipation in a world where random actors popping up out of nowhere, full of sound and fury, signifying nothing, that involves unintelligible stuff happening with no rhyme, meaning, plot, climax, or resolution is actually not so out of place. Hell, I have that happen all the time. Life is (semi-)like that-we tell stories that matter to us in a world that just can't make sense because there's so much unrelated stuff in it.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness evokes a great sense of verisimilitude because it honestly feels like how a real world of supernatural forces that go up to the cosmic level would act. THere's no answers for the world, and in the end it doesn't matter anyways, because my life-my stupid, tiny, significant, brilliant life- exists down here in the dust and mire and not in the eyes in the dark we call a starry night sky. I favor stories that look the nihilism of cosmic horror in the eye and punch it until it pays attention, thereby robbing it of power-but that's meaningless if the universe actually has enough coherent meaning to actually amount to something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-03-2015, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T09:43:04-08:00","id":426642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=426021#post426021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what happens when a Deceived Mummy enters the Inferno, starts throwing around Utterances with the aid of an Astra, and his target is a God-Machine Demon whose Cover is a former Promethean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, the ST gets a headache.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T13:07:04-08:00","id":426904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=425868#post425868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And this right here is why the final episodes of Battlestar Galactica blew..</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree here... Battlestar Galactica was never shy about telling you how it would end... They did so throughout the entire series, time and again...<br /> I enjoyed the hell out of it nonetheless... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T13:14:35-08:00","id":426911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=426904#post426904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree here... Battlestar Galactica was never shy about telling you how it would end... They did so throughout the entire series, time and again...<br /> I enjoyed the hell out of it nonetheless... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They told me they weren't going to answer any of the big questions about God, the Lords of Kobol, the afterlife, the time cycle, or any of the rest?<br /> <br /> I must have missed that part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T13:16:42-08:00","id":426916,"title":"","content":"Apparently So... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T02:31:34-07:00","id":986013,"title":"","content":"Old thread that went off topic into the meta debate about whether people should try to reconcile things or not. (Spoiler - I'm on the side that thinks it's fun to do so and that players enjoy knowing there's something behind the curtain). But Xenu's Paradox said something earlier about how the CofD setting almost appeared to be multiple timelines shattered through some catastrophic event on the part of the splat responsible. What if that were literally true and the only way to put things together again were to line up the biggest overlapping parts as your starting point. I'll try to explain what I mean.<br /> <br /> Imagine a tapestry. Maybe it's five tapestries, maybe it's one. Maybe they're stories, not tapestries. But whatever the number and whatever they are, you're trying to stich it back together into a coherent whole. Like unifying Roman and Greek gods or trying to reconcile two accounts of an ancient war, you start with the big points of similarity. Here is a Beowulf like figure that appears very similar in both tapestries - in fact, the way they're posed, the colours used - they look almost the same. Stitch here - sew them together. There is an island. The writing above one says 'Mu', the other says 'Atlantis'. But there's a giant wave sewn in gold and azure depicted rising over both. That looks almost good enough to join. There's a hole here, something was ripped out. Large, there's a bit of grey remaining. It could be a wolf or it could be a watchtower. Okay - leave that, we need to find the tear. Ah - here it is! What did this? A fire? An animal? Doesn't matter, this is the edge or it. Of them. This is where the tapestry was torn (if it ever was a single tapestry). An event, a cataclysmic event, caused by some mortal sin - pride, ignorance, jealousy... It's huge and it's common to all of the stories. That's where we put our first thread. It's the overlap in the two accounts of the war, it's the Zeus equals Jupiter. We stictch. And we keep on stiching.<br /> <br /> Nothing quite lines up perfectly - particularly not people's accounts of events - because those events are a construct of trying to reconcile different worlds. That's what the God Machine <b>is</b>. It's the weaver that is trying to repair the damage. Blindly and experimentally and without reference to morality or happiness or what the picture was originally intended to be. But it sees two edges that look like they can be joined and it does so. People may argue over what &quot;really happened&quot; but the God Machine has already put its own version in place and moved on. That's why Demons can slip between personas swapping and retaining pieces of people's lives - because they're the needles of the God Machine. Misplaced ones perhaps, broken ones probably. But they're needles that sew the threads of the world. Is the Dark Mother an ancient mage who ascended to the Supernal? Maybe she was once or maybe she wasn't, or maybe there were two similar figures that have become one figure now that history has been crudely joined. This is why sometimes the God Machine will create what people think are alternate timelines. It joins two sections together and for a little while the picture is different. But then it realizes this doesn't work. Maybe there's a better fit over there, maybe the edges didn't line up as well as it intended putting a wolf's head on that man over there. So it unpicks and tries again. The God Machine isn't intelligent, it is smart. It cannot design, it can only see. And it feels its way along blindly, trying and trying to repair.<br /> <br /> Was it once a single, bright tapestry that tore apart? Pieces missing so that even when joined together at last you can still see the damage, still characters and events missing from the tale? Was it always five different tales now being clumsily but so skillfully joined into one? What is the Abyss - things that have yet to be woven in? Loose threads and torn fragments of the picture that can never be found a place? What is the Supernal? Another part of the picture or the picture on the jigsaw box that the God Machine or the Exarchs look at as they try to assemble the world to look like it. Do the Exarchs know they are missing pieces? Does the God Machine care that it is?<br /> <br /> To pull back from the description back to game level stuff, the thing I like about this idea is that the inconsistencies and different takes on things have an <b>in-game</b> explanation. It's not just a storyteller being okay with the fact that things don't quite line up, it's an explanation you could give to characters in the game, it's an explanation that you could provide to your players at the end of a three year epic cross-over game and they would be satisfied. I have never been and never will be satisfied with the approach that there need be nothing behind the curtain. Once a player or GM acknowledges that it's all sound and fury signifying nothing, then exploring of mysteries becomes devalued. We might never find Moby Dick, but knowing that Moby Dick isn't out there makes searching for him much less satisfying. We do not need to know what is down in the depths to enjoy searching, but we cannot know that they are empty. Players expect their storyteller to know the truth in any mystery and are less satisfied if she does not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}